cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "An open dataset of soil compaction tests"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it and the original sources listed in data/sources.csv."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Youwai"
    given-names: "Sompote"
    affiliation: "King Mongkut's University of Technology Thonburi"
    email: "sompote.you@kmutt.ac.th"
  - family-names: "Phutthananon"
    given-names: "Chana"
    affiliation: "King Mongkut's University of Technology Thonburi"
abstract: >-
  2,854 Proctor compaction tests assembled from six public sources, each record
  complete in the index properties required for modelling and each carrying the
  compactive energy stated by its source, spanning four Proctor energy levels
  from 355 to 2,693 kJ/m3 and both sides of the coarse/fine boundary. Released
  alongside a wider pool of 7,273 quality-controlled records and 90 digitised
  compaction curves comprising 1,048 measured water-content / dry-density
  points. Every record carries its originating source so that evaluation can
  respect provenance. Trained gradient-boosted weights for maximum dry density
  and optimum moisture content are released with the data, together with a
  command-line predictor and the out-of-fold accuracy of both.
keywords:
  - soil compaction
  - Proctor test
  - maximum dry density
  - optimum moisture content
  - compactive energy
  - compaction curve
  - geotechnical engineering
  - open data
  - machine learning
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: 2026-09-03
version: "2.2.0"
